---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { SITE } from "../lib/site";
import { PATHS, linkClass } from "../lib/links";
import { withBase } from "../lib/base";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy | FFL Accelerator"
  description="What the contact form, email popup, and analytics collect, and how to ask for deletion."
  path="/privacy/"
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6 sm:py-16">
    <p class="text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-gold">
      Privacy
    </p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-white">
      Privacy
    </h1>
    <div class="mt-6 space-y-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-300">
      <p>
        Coriolis, LLC. {SITE.street}, {SITE.locality}, {SITE.region}
        {SITE.postal}. Phone
        <a class={linkClass} href={SITE.phoneHref}>{SITE.phone}</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        The contact form collects your name, company, email, phone, website,
        topic, and message. The email popup collects an email address.
      </p>
      <p>
        The first time you land here, we store the landing page and any
        first-touch campaign parameters (UTM fields and ad click IDs) in
        localStorage on your browser for 30 days. That helps us see which page
        and which ad the conversation started from. It stays on this device.
      </p>
      <p>
        If a measurement ID is configured for this site, pages load Google
        Analytics 4. That records how the site is used. It is not required to
        send the contact form.
      </p>
      <p>
        Form and popup submissions go to Coriolis, LLC's internal systems so we
        can reply. We do not sell your data.
      </p>
      <p>
        To ask for deletion, call
        <a class={linkClass} href={SITE.phoneHref}>{SITE.phone}</a>
        or use the
        <a class={linkClass} href={withBase(PATHS.contact)}>contact form</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
